        <!-- SLIDE 01: Solar Control -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide of-ftype-active" data-slide="0">
          <img src="/images/re-slider-solar.jpg" alt="Solar control window film on Philadelphia retail storefront" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">01</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Solar Control Film</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Reduces solar heat gain and glare while maintaining storefront visibility. Available in a range of visible light transmissions to match your display strategy and brand aesthetic.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will it change how my display windows look from the street?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Spectrally selective films like 3M Prestige 70 are virtually invisible from the exterior — they add no tint, no reflection, and no color shift. Your merchandise stays fully visible. We bring samples on every site visit so you can see exactly how the film looks on your glass before we install anything.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Will my merchandise colors still look accurate under film?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — high-VLT solar control films (70%+ visible light transmission) have minimal effect on how colors read inside your store. Customers won't perceive a difference in lighting quality. If color accuracy is critical for your product category, we'll recommend films with a color rendering index specifically tested for retail environments.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What's the difference between tinted and spectrally selective film?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Tinted films reduce heat and glare by blocking visible light — which also darkens your store interior slightly. Spectrally selective films use nano-ceramic technology to block infrared heat and UV while passing most visible light. For retail storefronts where lighting and display visibility matter, spectrally selective is almost always the right choice. 3M Prestige 70 rejects 50% of solar heat while maintaining 70% visible light — best of both worlds.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Get a solar control estimate →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 02: Security / Safety -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide" data-slide="1">
          <img src="/images/re-slider-security.jpg" alt="Security window film on Philadelphia retail jewelry store or boutique" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">02</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Security &amp; Safety Film</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Reinforces retail glass against smash-and-grab attacks, accidental impact, and severe weather. Holds panes together on breakage to deter entry and protect occupants from glass shards.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How does security film actually slow a smash-and-grab?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Standard retail glass shatters in one hit. Security film bonds to the glass substrate and holds the pane in the frame even after it breaks — the intruder has to keep striking to get through, which takes time, creates noise, and draws attention. Most smash-and-grab attempts are opportunistic and rely on speed. A film-reinforced window changes the risk calculation significantly.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can security film qualify for an insurance discount?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Some commercial property insurers recognize documented physical security upgrades when reviewing premiums. Security window film is a measurable hardening measure — we provide written documentation of the film product, certification standards met (including ANSI Z97.1 for applicable grades), and installation date. We recommend you share this with your broker.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does it protect against internal glass breakage too?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes. Security film prevents flying glass shards regardless of what causes the break — an accidental impact, a weather event, or a forced entry attempt. For retailers in older Philadelphia buildings with large single-pane storefronts, this secondary benefit (occupant safety from shards) is often as valuable as the security deterrence.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Get a security film estimate →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 03: Decorative & Branded -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide" data-slide="2">
          <img src="/images/re-slider-decorative.jpg" alt="Decorative branded window film on Philadelphia retail storefront" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">03</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Decorative &amp; Branded Film</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Custom frosted, patterned, and printed films for storefront branding, fitting room privacy, and interior partitions. Apply your logo, a seasonal design, or a brand pattern directly to glass. Available in frosted, patterned, or custom-printed finishes.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can we print our store logo or seasonal artwork on the film?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — digitally printed window film lets you put any design directly on your storefront or interior glass. We work from your supplied artwork or coordinate with your designer. Custom printed films are fully removable, so you can swap seasonal campaigns or update your branding without replacing glass or hiring a painter.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What happens to decorative film when we rebrand or move?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Decorative and printed window films are designed to be removable. Removal leaves the glass clean with no permanent adhesive residue when done properly — which is why we recommend professional removal. For retail tenants, this means you can restore the glass to its original condition when your lease ends.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How long does decorative film last in a retail environment?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Interior decorative films typically last 7–10 years under normal conditions. Exterior-facing decorative films see more UV and weather exposure, which shortens longevity — most exterior decorative films are rated 3–5 years. We'll specify the right product and warranty for your specific application during the site consultation.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Explore decorative options →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 04: Privacy / Frosted -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide" data-slide="3">
          <img src="/images/re-slider-privacy.jpg" alt="Privacy frosted window film in Philadelphia retail fitting room" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">04</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Privacy &amp; Frosted Film</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">One-way daytime privacy, frosted glass effects, and controlled light diffusion for fitting rooms, back-of-house partitions, and street-level windows in sensitive retail categories.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does one-way privacy film work during evening hours?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>One-way mirror film relies on a brightness differential — it's reflective from the outside when exterior light is brighter than interior light. After dark, when interior lights are on, the effect reverses and visibility from outside increases. For evening privacy in fitting rooms or street-level windows, frosted film is the right choice — it provides consistent privacy 24/7 regardless of lighting conditions.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Can frosted film be applied to fitting room glass doors?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Absolutely — fitting room glass doors and sidelights are one of the most common retail applications for frosted film. We typically apply film from approximately 18 inches above the floor to the top of the glass panel, maintaining a clear strip at the bottom (for safety/visibility) and full privacy where it matters. Custom cut heights are available.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is frosted film the same as etched or sandblasted glass?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Frosted film creates a visually identical effect to acid-etched or sandblasted glass at a fraction of the cost — and unlike etched glass, it's completely removable. For retailers who want a premium architectural finish on glass partitions or storefront panels without permanently altering the glass, frosted film is the standard solution.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Explore privacy film options →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- SLIDE 05: Anti-Graffiti -->
        <div class="of-ftype__slide" data-slide="4">
          <img src="/images/re-slider-antigraffiti.jpg" alt="Anti-graffiti window film protecting Philadelphia retail storefront glass" class="of-ftype__bg" />
          <div class="of-ftype__overlay"></div>
          <div class="of-ftype__content">
            <div class="of-ftype__step">05</div>
            <h2 class="of-ftype__title">Anti-Graffiti Film</h2>
            <p class="of-ftype__desc">Sacrificial surface film that protects storefront glass from etching, scratching, and spray paint. When vandalized, replace only the film — not the glass. Ideal for street-level retail in Center City and Kensington.</p>
            <div class="of-ftype__faq">
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Does it protect against both spray paint and glass etching?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Yes — anti-graffiti film is a sacrificial surface layer that takes the damage instead of your glass. Spray paint, acid etching, scratching, and marker all affect only the film. When vandalized, we remove and replace the film — which costs a small fraction of what glass replacement would. The underlying glass is untouched.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How quickly can vandalized film be replaced?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Film replacement is significantly faster than glass replacement — no specialty glass orders, no lead times, no building permits required. For most standard retail storefront panels, film removal and re-application can be completed in one visit. We prioritize turnaround for anti-graffiti clients to minimize the time vandalism is visible to customers.</div>
              </div>
              <div class="of-ftype__faq-item">
                <button class="of-ftype__faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Which Philadelphia neighborhoods see the highest graffiti rates?<span class="of-ftype__faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span></button>
                <div class="of-ftype__faq-a" hidden>Anti-graffiti film is most commonly requested by retailers in Center City, Kensington, Fishtown, and South Street — particularly ground-floor storefronts with large glass panels visible from the street. That said, graffiti and etching are genuinely unpredictable, and retailers in lower-risk areas install it too as a low-cost insurance policy against a surprisingly expensive repair.</div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <a href="/contact/" class="of-ftype__cta">Get an anti-graffiti estimate →</a>
          </div>
        </div>

